# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via Keycloak:** configured automatically on first deploy."
msgstr "**SSO via Keycloak:** beim ersten Deployment automatisch konfiguriert."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted `Remote-Email` header (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); an `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, adapted from [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n's own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2-proxy mit Auto-Provisioning:** V1 bietet allen Zugriff über den freigegebenen Keycloak OIDC-Client (Oauth2-Proxy-Rand). openresty leitet die authentifizierte Identität an n8n als Trusted weiter `Remote-Email` Kopf (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); ein `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` Skript (`files/hooks.js`, adaptiert aus [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) liest diesen Header, stellt einen lokalen n8n-Benutzer beim ersten Anmelden automatisch bereit und gibt das n8n-eigene Sitzungscookie aus - so dass jeder Keycloak-Benutzer direkt im Workflow-Editor landet, ohne einen zweiten, n8n-lokalen Anmeldeschritt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted ``Remote-Email`` header (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); an ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, adapted from `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n’s own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2-proxy mit Auto-Provisioning:** V1 bietet allen Zugriff über den freigegebenen Keycloak OIDC-Client (Oauth2-Proxy-Rand). openresty leitet die authentifizierte Identität an n8n als Trusted weiter ``Remote-Email`` Kopf (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); ein ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` Skript (``files/hooks.js``, adaptiert aus `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) liest diesen Header, stellt einen lokalen n8n-Benutzer beim ersten Anmelden automatisch bereit und gibt das n8n-eigene Sitzungscookie aus - so dass jeder Keycloak-Benutzer direkt im Workflow-Editor landet, ohne einen zweiten, n8n-lokalen Anmeldeschritt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM's own SAML login against Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall's SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to `/saml/acs` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak's realm descriptor by [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a `.onion` issuer is unresolvable directly. `/auth` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** ist SuiteCRMs eigenes SAML-Login gegen Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml))Kein Proxy davor. Nicht authentifizierte Anfragen trafen den SAML-Einstiegspunkt der Symfony-Firewall, der zu Keycloak weiterleitet; die Behauptung kommt zurück zu `/saml/acs` und richtet eine echte SuiteCRM-Sitzung ein, sodass die App ihre eigene authentifizierte Benutzeroberfläche einschließlich ihrer Anmeldesteuerung darstellt. Konten werden beim ersten Login aus der Assertion erstellt (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), und das IdP-Signierungszertifikat wird aus Keycloaks Realm-Deskriptor gelesen [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) beim boot, über den tor socks proxy, wenn der emittent eine zwiebel ist, weil ein. `.onion` Der Emittent ist direkt unlösbar. `/auth` bleibt als lokales Break-Glas-Login erreichbar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** ist SuiteCRMs eigenes SAML-Login gegen Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` bleibt als lokales Break-Glas-Login erreichbar."

