# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Cross-service probes (biber denied at prometheus, biber denied at matomo, dashboard tile reachability) are NOT part of the per-role biber persona. They live in the provider's own spec (`web-app-{prometheus,matomo,dashboard}/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`), parameterised once over the provider's `<NAME>_TARGET_ROLES_JSON` manifest. For the dashboard, the parameterised scenario delegates to `web-app-dashboard/files/playwright/dashboard-card-flow.js::runDashboardCardScenario(page, context, target)`, which owns the tile visibility / iframe-embed / \"Tab\" pop-out assertions in one SPOT."
msgstr "Cross-Service-Sonden (Biber verweigert bei Prometheus, Biber verweigert bei matomo, Dashboard-Kachel Erreichbarkeit) sind NICHT Teil der Pro-Rolle-Biber-Persona. Sie leben in der eigenen Spec des Anbieters (`web-app-{prometheus,matomo,dashboard}/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`), parametriert einmal gegenüber dem Anbieter `<NAME>_TARGET_ROLES_JSON` manifest. Für das Dashboard delegiert das parametrisierte Szenario `web-app-dashboard/files/playwright/dashboard-card-flow.js::runDashboardCardScenario(page, context, target)`, die die Kachel Sichtbarkeit / iframe-embed / \"Tab\" Pop-out-Behauptungen in einem SPOT besitzt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Cross-service probes are NOT part of the per-role administrator persona. Dashboard tile reachability is owned by `web-app-dashboard/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, which delegates the per-target body to the `runDashboardCardScenario` helper in `dashboard-card-flow.js` (tile visible → click loads in `#main iframe` → header \"Tab\" button pops the embed into a fresh browser tab). That helper is the SPOT for dashboard-tile mechanics; consumer specs MUST NOT reimplement any of those assertions. Prometheus admin-reach and scrape parity are owned by `web-app-prometheus/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. Matomo admin-reach and tracker presence are owned by `web-app-matomo/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. Each provider parameterises the assertion over its `<NAME>_TARGET_ROLES_JSON` manifest."
msgstr "Cross-Service-Sonden sind NICHT Teil der Per-Role Administrator Persona. Dashboard-Kachel Erreichbarkeit ist Eigentum von `web-app-dashboard/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, die die pro-Ziel-Körperschaft an die `runDashboardCardScenario` Helfer in `dashboard-card-flow.js` (Titel sichtbar → Clickloads in) `#main iframe` → Header \"Tab\"-Taste schaltet das Einbetten in einen frischen Browser-Tab. Dieser Helfer ist der SPOT für Dashboard-Kachelmechanik; Verbraucherspezifikationen MÜSSEN KEINE dieser Behauptungen wieder umsetzen. Prometheus Admin-Reach und Scrape Parity sind Eigentum von `web-app-prometheus/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. Matomo Admin-Reach und Tracker-Präsenz sind Eigentum von `web-app-matomo/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`. Jeder Anbieter parametrisiert die Aussage über seine `<NAME>_TARGET_ROLES_JSON` manifest."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Cross-service surface assertions (dashboard tile reachability, prometheus admin-reach and scrape parity, matomo admin-reach and tracker presence, biber-denied-at-prometheus, biber-denied-at-matomo) are owned by the provider's own spec. Each provider parameterises the assertion over its `<NAME>_TARGET_ROLES_JSON` manifest, rendered via `lookup('roles_with_service', '<svc>')`. Consumer roles' personas MUST NOT duplicate these probes."
msgstr "Cross-Service-Oberflächenbehauptungen (Dashboard-Erreichbarkeit, prometheus Admin-Reach und Scrape-Parität, matomo Admin-Reach und Tracker-Präsenz, biber-denied-at-prometheus, biber-denied-at-matomo) sind Eigentum der eigenen Spezifikation des Anbieters. Jeder Anbieter parametrisiert die Aussage über seine `<NAME>_TARGET_ROLES_JSON` Manifest, über `lookup('roles_with_service', '<svc>')`. Die Personas der Verbraucherrollen dürfen diese Sonden NICHT duplizieren."

