msgid "Inputs (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INFINITO_DOMAIN`` (the SPOT for the deployment domain; defined in ``default.env`` and exported by ``scripts/meta/env/load.sh``; the development inventory reads the same env var for the play's ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY``), ``HOSTS_ENTRY_IP`` (optional; address the domains map to, default ``127.0.0.1``)."
msgstr "Input (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INFINITO_DOMAIN`` (der SPOT für die Bereitstellungsdomäne; definiert in) ``default.env`` und ausgeführt von ``scripts/meta/env/load.sh``; das Entwicklungsinventar liest die gleiche env var für das Spiel ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY``, ``HOSTS_ENTRY_IP`` (optional; Adresse der Domains map to, standardmäßig) ``127.0.0.1``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INV_PATH`` (default ``/tmp/inv/devices.yml``). Optional ``INFINITO_APP_VARIANTS`` (consumed by ``derive_includes``)."
msgstr "Input (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INV_PATH`` (Standard) ``/tmp/inv/devices.yml``. Fakultativ ``INFINITO_APP_VARIANTS`` (verbraucht von) ``derive_includes``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs (env): ``INV_DIR`` — inventory dir holding ``host_vars/*.yml`` (default ``/tmp/inv``)."
msgstr "Input (env): ``INV_DIR`` — Inventar Dirholding ``host_vars/*.yml`` (Standard) ``/tmp/inv``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs (env): ``NFS_IP``, ``MGR_IP``, ``MGR``, ``OUT_PATH`` (default ``/tmp/swarm-nfs-extras.yml``), ``KEY_PATH`` (default ``/tmp/swarm-nfs-admin.key``). A second ed25519 keypair is generated at ``INFINITO_SWARM_BACKUP_KEY`` (SPOT: default.env) and its public half lands in ``users.backup.authorized_keys`` so the DR drill's backup host can pull over the ``user-backup`` ssh-wrapper. The ``applications`` block written into the extras file carries the ``local-2-device`` mount/target/source device paths, which is all the DR drill reads back from it. The deploy-facing overrides, including ``remote-2-local.backup_providers`` (derived per round from ``utils.tests.swarm.backup_repos``), are baked by the matrix orchestrator into the provisioner's host_vars merge (INFINITO_VARS_PAYLOAD), NOT into the extras file: extra-vars replace the whole inventory ``applications`` dict and would strip every generated credential. ``users`` carries the same hazard for the same reason, and its authorized_keys travel the same merge channel. The deploy-facing twin ``<OUT_PATH stem>.deploy.yml`` therefore carries everything except ``applications`` and ``users``."
msgstr "Inputs (env): ``NFS_IP``, ``MGR_IP``, ``MGR``, ``OUT_PATH`` (Ausfall ``/tmp/swarm-nfs-extras.yml``), ``KEY_PATH`` (Ausfall ``/tmp/swarm-nfs-admin.key``)Ein zweites ed25519 Schlüsselpaar wird bei ``INFINITO_SWARM_BACKUP_KEY`` (SPOT: default.env) und seine öffentliche Hälfte landet in ``users.backup.authorized_keys`` So kann der Backup-Host des DR-Bohrers den ``user-backup`` ssh-wrapper. Die ``applications`` Der in die Extras-Datei geschriebene Block trägt die ``local-2-device`` mount/target/source Gerätepfade, was alles ist, was der dr-bohrer von ihm zurückliest. Die Deployment-facing Overrides, einschließlich ``remote-2-local.backup_providers`` (pro Runde abgeleitet von ``utils.tests.swarm.backup_repos``), werden vom Matrix-Orchestrator in die Provisioner gebacken host_vars Verschmelzung (INFINITO_VARS_PAYLOAD), NICHT in die Extras-Datei: Extra-vars ersetzen das gesamte Inventar ``applications`` diktiert und würde jede generierte Berechtigung abstreifen. ``users`` trägt die gleiche Gefahr aus dem gleichen Grund und seine authorized_keys den gleichen Merge-Kanal durchlaufen. Der auf den Einsatz ausgerichtete Zwilling ``<OUT_PATH stem>.deploy.yml`` und trägt alles außer ``applications`` und ``users``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs come from the merged application config (``services.<key>.image`` and ``services.<key>.version``). ``image=`` and ``version=`` keyword overrides bypass those values for ad-hoc references (e.g. side-car init containers that do not appear in the services map)."
msgstr "Inputs stammen aus der Mergered Application Config (``services.<key>.image`` und ``services.<key>.version``). ``image=`` und ``version=`` Keyword Overrides umgehen diese Werte für Ad-hoc-Referenzen (z. B. Side-Car-Init-Container, die nicht in der Dienstleistungskarte erscheinen)."

